49750, "input": 52381, "output": 110}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 54284, "other": 423, "system": 32605, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 57206}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 158915}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "18a5e529-0e73-5daa-9b93-6b38e4c6f6d7", "at": 1795625809.992242, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 22256, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "47d688c2e463394970e35722e3222e85", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "7450730f-9bdd-5081-91be-0ba4327ed2be", "at": 1795625811.2674713, "until": 1795625811.2899477, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 22257, "layer": "worker", "category": "thinking", "kind": "session.agent_thought_chunk", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": null, "execution_id": "47d688c2e463394970e35722e3222e85", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "thinking", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "thinking (9 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "85d2ab53-4a22-572f-8bb2-81ff62d147ed", "at": 1795625811.2926714, "until": 1795625811.4588861, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 22266, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "47d688c2e463394970e35722e3222e85", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_017Em5iNVaLjTXaz6gkrEj4k", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/repo; sed -n 77,120p VENUE.md", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/repo; sed -n 77,120p VENUE.md"]], "output": "```console\n## 4. Anonymity and what a delivery of this study must not contain **[venue]**\n\n- The paper is submitted anonymised: no names, institutions, acknowledgments or links that identify the authors.\n  Own earlier work is cited in the third person. This applies to supplementary code. With the style's default option\n  (no `final`, no `preprint`) the style anonymises the author block, adds line numbers and prints the\n  \"Submitted to ... Do not distribute\" footer. **Use the default (submission) mode**, not `final`.\n- Links to external material must allow anonymous browsing. Do not cite line numbers.\n- A non-anonymous preprint would use the `preprint` option, never `final`. Neither is needed for this delivery.\n\n## 5. Required parts besides the body **[venue]**\n\n- **Paper checklist, mandatory, 16 items**, in `checklist.tex`, loaded by `\\input{checklist.tex}` after the references and\n  the appendix; it does not count toward the nine pages. \"Papers not including the checklist will be desk rejected.\"\n  Answer with the macros `\\answerYes{}`, `\\answerNo{}`, `\\answerNA{}` and a 1-2 sentence justification each; **do not modify the\n  questions or the guidelines; delete only the instruction block and keep the heading \"NeurIPS Paper Checklist\"**.\n  The items: Claims; Limitations; Theory assumptions and proofs; Experimental result reproducibility; Open access to data\n  and code; Experimental setting/details; Experiment statistical significance; Experiments compute resources; Code of ethics;\n  Broader impacts; Safeguards; Licenses for existing assets; New assets; Crowdsourcing and research with human subjects;\n  IRB approvals; Declaration of LLM usage. \"Answering No is typically not grounds for rejection\".\n  What this study has to answer honestly (flags for `paper-repo` and `experiment-repo`):\n  * *Licences for existing assets*: MTEB results are CC0-1.0; the Open LLM Leaderboard table and the LiveBench judgments carry **no declared dataset licence**; the HELM\n    scenario data licences are \"not checked item by item\" (`data.md`). The answer must say so; do not write \"Yes, licensed\" unless\n    verified.\n  * *LLM usage (item 16)*: \"described in the experimental setup if it is an important, original, or non-standard component\".\n    Here the research itself was carried out by AI agents; the answer must be truthful, and the paper should say it once\n    where the method/setup is described. This is for `paper-repo` to word.\n  * *Statistical significance*: the family-clustered bootstrap CIs the Brief fixes answer it. *Compute resources*: CPU only, hours.\n  * *Crowdsourcing / IRB*: not applicable (no human subjects; public leaderboards).\n- **Broader impacts**: no section required; a discussion, if any, may sit anywhere and counts inside the nine pages.\n- Camera-ready only (not needed here): funding disclosure in `ack`, lay summary.\n- The submission form (not visible to me) holds a contribution-type choice, a confidential LLM-usage select and a LLM-review opt-in; no role fills it.\n\n## 6. Supplementary material **[venue]**\n\n- Text appendices: in the same PDF after the references. They may hold proofs, derivations, full tables, audits.\n- **Code and data: one anonymised ZIP (`.zip`/`.tgz`/`.gz`), at most 100 MB**; no written appendix inside it; reviewers need not open it.\n  Required: training/evaluation code and a dependency specification; \"ideally self-contained and executable; otherwise\n  explain why\". For `experiment-repo`: the code package must fit 100 MB *without* the data (data is fetched by script from\n  the pinned versions in `data.md`; the MTEB history clone is ~0.6 GB and cannot ship). Anonymise (no names, no\n  institution URLs, no licence text carrying a name).\n- The objective additionally asks for the reproduction notes (environment and versions, data steps and versions, seeds,\n  commands and expected times, which script makes each table and figure); these are the objective's requirement and\n  satisfy the venue's checklist items 4-6 and 5.\n`\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "a8d7998f-a779-5367-aba4-7a0769da0dcd", "at": 1795625811.3209066, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 22268, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "47d688c2e463394970e35722e3222e85", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "34b1a96c-f03f-5a78-bfde-c79b41a4adce", "at": 1795625811.7776837, "until": 1795625817.7147624, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 22272, "layer": "worker", "category": "model", "kind": "model.request", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "47d688c2e463394970e35722e3222e85", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "completed", "label": "model → completed", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "model request → completed in 5.2s (instruction ✓, activation ✓) [max_tokens 128000, output_config.effort high, thinking.display summarized, thinking.type adaptive]; gateway set thinking.display; called Bash ×1; tokens in 53,942 (cached 52,379, 97%, written 1,561 (1h 1,561, 5m 0)) out 515; requested claude-sonnet-5-5; served claude-sonnet-5-5 ×1", "model": {"requests": 1, "attempts": [{"outcome": "stream-ended", "category": "completed", "seconds": 5.205992433009669, "served": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"]}], "probes": {"instruction_present": true, "activation_present": true}, "side": false, "subagent": false, "provider": null, "requested": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "served": {"claude-sonnet-5-5": 1}, "parameters": {"max_tokens": 128000, "output_config.effort": "high", "thinking.display": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": null, "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 1561, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 1561, "cached_input": 52379, "input": 53942, "output": 515}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 55817, "other": 423, "system": 32684, "tool_definitions": 14397, "